commit 79643b97b293facdb43f9477d50219f8b33a4ed0
Author: ai4sci-z <jiaogali2580@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 6 18:27:23 2026 +0800

    fix(sim): make external-nav exploration reach takeoff end-to-end (clean-repro validated)
    
    Reproduced from a fresh upstream clone (09a5aa4) on jazzy; fixed one blocker
    at a time until the vehicle physically lifts off (SIM ground-truth alt rose
    ~0.53m, motors 1864-1950 PWM). Bugs (each stops the run cold for any user):
    
    1. exploration_workflow_runtime.py.tmpl: literal %% -> % (text/template does
       not Sprintf; rendered script fails py_compile with SyntaxError).
    2. backends.py: omit empty launch args (ROS2 rejects empty name:=, jazzy too).
    3. slam.go + defaults.go: SlamBackend IMU output topic must differ from the
       /imu bridge source, else IMU echo -> cartographer aborts (Non-sorted data).
    4. navlab_models.go + parm files: RNGFND1_MIN_CM/MAX_CM/GNDCLEAR are pre-4.5
       names ignored by current firmware -> MIN defaults 0.20m, rejects the 0.095m
       sim reading (Rangefinder: No Data). Use RNGFND1_MIN/MAX/GNDCLR.
    5. parm + defaults.go: DISARM_DELAY 0 and longer readiness so the vehicle is
       not auto-disarmed while the external-nav EKF converges.
    6. parm: EK3_SRC1_POSZ baro so an altitude estimate exists before origin.
    7. fcu_controller_runtime.py.tmpl (KEY): do not forward exploration intent to
       the FCU until takeoff is complete. Before takeoff the stationary hold intent
       is sent as cmd_vel/local-position setpoint and overrides the GUIDED takeoff
       climb (CTUN.DAlt pinned to current alt), so it never lifts off -> takeoff
       never ok -> controller never ready -> workflow keeps sending hold -> deadlock.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

